{# The component gallery the Preset screen renders (ticket 30).

   Wiki source, not HTML: it goes through MarkdownFormatterService exactly as a page body
   does, so what a preset is judged against is what the wiki will actually produce. Writing
   the expected HTML by hand here would make the preview agree with itself rather than with
   the renderer.

   `{% verbatim %}`, because the whole point is the literal `{{action}}` syntax -- Twig would
   otherwise read every component as one of its own expressions.

   Each block is titled with the markup that produced it, in the wiki's own syntax. That is
   deliberate: it is language-neutral, so the gallery needs no translation, and it makes the
   preview double as a syntax reference -- you see the component and the line that draws it. #}
