{# `flat`, and it is load-bearing: what this file produces is WIKI SOURCE, and Markdown
   reads any line indented by four spaces as a code block. The presentation templates emit
   indented markup, so including one raw put the second card onwards inside a `<pre><code>`
   -- a gallery that rendered exactly one card and printed the other five as source, while
   every class name a test could look for was still present. Trimming each line leaves the
   markup intact and leaves Markdown nothing to mistake for code. #}
{% macro flat(html) %}{{ html|split("\n")|map(line => line|trim)|join("\n")|raw }}{% endmacro %}
{% import _self as source %}

